WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.800
Subsidies covering 550,000 hectares increase Morocco's groundwater use instead of conserving it.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.740
This is unintended consequences, episode 185.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.600
In 2007, Morocco launched the National Program of Water Savings in Irrigation under the

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.600
Green Morocco Plan, supported by World Bank financing, and claimed savings exceeding 1 billion

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.380
cubic meters.

00:00:23.426 --> 00:00:29.786
Marcel Cooper and colleagues at Seerad traced the policy routes to the 1980s and 1990s, when

00:00:29.786 --> 00:00:34.926
When state planners in large-scale schemes such as TADLA sought to stabilize medium-sized

00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:41.506
farms through surface water delivery and industrial crops, by the mid-2000s declining rainfall and

00:00:41.506 --> 00:00:46.646
growing demand had produced visible groundwater depletion and officials viewed drip conversion

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.206
as the logical next step.

00:00:48.846 --> 00:00:54.886
Subsidies climbed from earlier levels of 60% to 80% to 100% for micro irrigation equipment,

00:00:55.486 --> 00:00:56.806
wells and reservoirs.

00:00:56.806 --> 00:01:01.686
Policy makers reasoned that higher application efficiency would reduce the volume of water

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:06.986
needed per hectare while raising yields and rural incomes, in line with the green Morocco

00:01:06.986 --> 00:01:11.606
plans emphasis on agricultural intensification and export competitiveness.

00:01:12.066 --> 00:01:16.846
At the time, remote sensing data and field studies had not yet quantified how farmers

00:01:16.846 --> 00:01:21.406
would respond, so the decision rested on the premise that technical efficiency gains

00:01:21.406 --> 00:01:24.826
would translate directly into lower basin wide withdrawals.

00:01:24.826 --> 00:01:30.346
Officials had watched surface water quotas shrink in dry years, and concluded that replacing

00:01:30.346 --> 00:01:35.346
open-channel flooding with pressurized pipes, emitters, and on-farm reservoirs would

00:01:35.346 --> 00:01:38.846
stretch every cubic meter further without new dams or transfers.

00:01:39.546 --> 00:01:44.266
The capital grants were also expected to lift small and medium holdings into higher-value

00:01:44.266 --> 00:01:48.866
fruit and vegetable production, improving food security and foreign exchange earnings

00:01:48.866 --> 00:01:49.686
from exports.

00:01:49.686 --> 00:01:55.944
reports. Between 2007 and 2008, the government scaled subsidy rates sharply and streamlined

00:01:55.944 --> 00:02:01.824
approvals for turnkey projects that included ponds and private wells. By the end of 2008,

00:02:02.084 --> 00:02:07.964
roughly 163,000 hectares had been equipped, concentrated in fruit tree zones of the Tadla

00:02:07.964 --> 00:02:14.204
perimeter and the El-Haus plain. Early monitoring recorded higher biomass per hectare and lower

00:02:14.204 --> 00:02:19.244
reported water deliveries at the scheme level, and program documents presented those figures

00:02:19.244 --> 00:02:20.824
as evidence of conservation.

00:02:21.364 --> 00:02:26.364
The World Bank's large-scale irrigation modernization project, backed by a loan of

00:02:26.364 --> 00:02:31.224
$150 million, conditioned further support on collective conversion to drip.

00:02:31.844 --> 00:02:36.444
Local agricultural offices promoted drip as a way for farmers to maintain production

00:02:36.444 --> 00:02:38.804
even when surface water quotas fell short.

00:02:39.424 --> 00:02:44.904
A 2009 Irrigation Association paper noted that average installation costs reached about

00:02:44.904 --> 00:02:52.084
$5,725 per hectare, with 70% of projects also building on-farm reservoirs.

00:02:52.604 --> 00:02:56.284
Proponents highlighted the prospect of 20-50% water savings.

00:02:56.864 --> 00:03:01.444
Few contemporaneous reports tracked whether the freed water stayed in the aquifer or was

00:03:01.444 --> 00:03:02.224
applied elsewhere.

00:03:02.944 --> 00:03:08.124
Application forms required only proof of equipment purchase and basic soil tests, and

00:03:08.124 --> 00:03:12.884
no clause limited how many additional hectares a recipient could bring under irrigation once

00:03:12.884 --> 00:03:14.124
the system was installed.

00:03:15.116 --> 00:03:20.776
An agricultural water management paper from 2017 reported that aquifer overdraft in the

00:03:20.776 --> 00:03:26.256
affected basins reached 1 billion cubic meters per year, even as drip coverage expanded.

00:03:26.856 --> 00:03:32.436
In the El-Haus perimeter, remote sensing analysis funded by the Global Water Security and Sanitation

00:03:32.436 --> 00:03:39.056
Partnership, GWSP, showed that water consumption per hectare did not decline once drip systems

00:03:39.056 --> 00:03:44.336
were installed, as farmers increased crop density and planted more water-intensive varieties.

00:03:45.016 --> 00:03:51.476
Marcel Cooper's 2012 analysis of 40 years in the tadla scheme found that larger and medium-sized

00:03:51.476 --> 00:03:57.676
holdings, which captured 36% of farms, used new access to groundwater to lease additional

00:03:57.676 --> 00:04:00.516
land and diversify into higher-value orchards.

00:04:00.976 --> 00:04:05.776
Because drip-reduced surface water losses that had previously recharged shallow aquifers,

00:04:05.776 --> 00:04:09.216
Net recharge fell while private tube well-pumping rows.

00:04:09.576 --> 00:04:15.796
The 2017 Sierra ad book chapter on North African cases traced how the same efficiency narrative

00:04:15.796 --> 00:04:20.676
persisted in policy documents, despite the absence of base-and-scale metering that would

00:04:20.676 --> 00:04:22.256
have revealed the expansion effect.

00:04:22.836 --> 00:04:28.696
Farmers who received 100% subsidies for wells and ponds faced no volumetric limit on extraction,

00:04:29.236 --> 00:04:32.176
so the marginal cost of adding irrigated area dropped.

00:04:32.176 --> 00:04:38.296
Informal land markets accelerated, small holders without capital for wells rented out parcels,

00:04:38.696 --> 00:04:42.076
and deeper aquifers began to be tapped as shallow tables dropped.

00:04:42.636 --> 00:04:48.516
By the time the 2017 Elsevier study quantified the paradox, the pattern had already locked

00:04:48.516 --> 00:04:50.956
in across multiple over-exploited basins.

00:04:51.436 --> 00:04:56.916
If a hectare previously received 8,000 cubic meters under flood irrigation, and now required

00:04:56.916 --> 00:05:02.996
only 5,000 under drip, the 3,000 cubic meters saved could irrigate another 6 tenths of a

00:05:02.996 --> 00:05:08.616
hectare of the same crop, or support a shift to citrus or vegetables that demanded 9,000 cubic

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:14.896
meters per hectare. Without an overall extraction cap, that extra hectare or that extra crop was

00:05:14.896 --> 00:05:20.196
planted. Larger operators captured most of the subsidy because those operators could finance

00:05:20.196 --> 00:05:26.236
the remaining 20% or the reservoir component, while smaller farms stayed on surface water or

00:05:26.236 --> 00:05:29.316
rented land out, concentrating groundwater rights.

00:05:29.776 --> 00:05:34.916
As recharge from surface losses declined, the same volume of pumping lowered water tables

00:05:34.916 --> 00:05:40.116
faster, forcing some farmers to deepen wells and raising energy costs that higher value

00:05:40.116 --> 00:05:41.576
output partly offset.

00:05:42.495 --> 00:05:48.635
Subsequent World Bank and GWSP evaluations in the 2020s acknowledged that measured water

00:05:48.635 --> 00:05:51.655
consumption had not fallen in line with earlier projections.

00:05:51.655 --> 00:05:51.855
operations.

00:05:52.115 --> 00:05:57.835
The large-scale irrigation modernization project continued, yet added components for monitoring

00:05:57.835 --> 00:06:02.455
actual evapotranspiration rather than relying on theoretical savings.

00:06:03.115 --> 00:06:08.455
No nationwide rollback of the subsidy structure occurred, and newer guidance emphasized pairing

00:06:08.455 --> 00:06:11.195
drip conversion with enforceable extraction permits.

00:06:11.815 --> 00:06:17.055
In the Tadla and El-Haus zones, some collective schemes began experimenting with collective

00:06:17.055 --> 00:06:19.975
well-management, though enforcement remained uneven.

00:06:19.975 --> 00:06:25.395
Aquifer levels in the most intensively converted perimeters continue to decline through the early

00:06:25.395 --> 00:06:31.395
2020s, prompting calls for volumetric pricing that had not been part of the original program design.

00:06:31.955 --> 00:06:37.415
Pilot programs now require satellite verification of cropped area alongside drip installation,

00:06:37.815 --> 00:06:41.995
but uptake of these paired rules has been slower than the original equipment grants.

00:06:43.155 --> 00:06:46.955
Any new efficiency program can be tested before funds are dispersed

00:06:46.955 --> 00:06:52.255
first, for a binding limit on aggregate extraction rather than a promise of savings per hectare.

00:06:52.795 --> 00:06:57.635
Draftors of the next arid region incentive can put that cap in the first eligibility rule,

00:06:58.095 --> 00:06:59.475
ahead of any equipment grant.

00:07:00.155 --> 00:07:04.095
Officials can run that test on paper before a single emitter is subsidized.

00:07:04.675 --> 00:07:09.735
Satellite verification of cropped area belongs in that same first rule if expansion is meant

00:07:09.735 --> 00:07:11.475
to be seen before it is paid for.

00:07:11.475 --> 00:07:16.135
Moreover, environmental intelligence tracks how satellite verification of cropped area

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:18.835
is written into payment rules across dry landscapes.

00:07:19.555 --> 00:07:23.835
How might current water saving incentives and other arid regions avoid repeating that

00:07:23.835 --> 00:07:24.555
measurement gap?

00:07:25.195 --> 00:07:26.855
And that's where today's story leaves us.

00:07:27.295 --> 00:07:30.735
If it changed how you see one everyday decision, that's the whole point.

00:07:31.255 --> 00:07:34.955
